      "problem": "$2x+4y+5x-2y-4=${{field-1}}\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$y\\,-$\n{{field-3}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we group the like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+4y+5x-2y-4 & = \\\\ {{2x+5x}_{⏟}}_{x\\text{ terms}}+{{4y-2y}_{⏟}}_{y\\text{ terms}}-4 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2x+5x}_{⏟}\\,+\\,{4y-2y}_{⏟}\\,-\\,4 & = \\\\ (2+5)x+(4-2)y-4 & = \\\\ 7\\,x+2\\,y-4 & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
